    {
      "Seq": 20,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Village",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 6800,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I sense a creature, a large white goose hissing. His neck stretched, alert, warning with each breath. A kinship to beasts, I read the readiness in his stance. I scent the tension in the air, the horse\u0027s tail flicking a warning, and I see three stone steps ready to mount, a beast\u0027s readiness palpable in the soft earth. I notice the village stocks, their grim set oak, the leg-holes polished sharp by use. It smells of restraint and fear, a warning in the way they stand, the coldness of iron against skin.",
